# ~9 GB of firmware images, renders and audio. Deliberately untracked:
# a fresh clone has the code and the documentation, not the data.
# `git clean -xdf` WOULD DELETE ALL OF IT. Back it up.
# No trailing slash: `data/` matches only a real directory, so a SYMLINK
# named `data` -- pointing at a shared data tree on another volume or in
# a sibling checkout, which is a supported setup -- showed up as
# untracked and `git add -A` would have committed an absolute path from
# somebody's machine into a public repository.
data
# ...with one exception: the reference tune in data/midi/, which is ours --
# Beethoven's melody, public domain, written by a script on 2026-10-20 -- and
# is what `render --midi ode_to_joy.mid` and `mfreak play` are compared with.
# Git cannot re-include a file under an excluded directory, so the directory
# itself is re-included (`!data/`, a trailing slash matches only a real
# directory, so a `data` SYMLINK stays ignored by the line above) and then
# everything in it is excluded again except that one file. Checked both
# ways: a real data/ tree adds only the .mid; a symlink adds nothing.
!data/
data/*
!data/midi/
data/midi/*
!data/midi/ode_to_joy.mid

# Build artifacts referenced by the long-running comparison tests.
artifacts/

# Never commit a firmware payload, a patched image or a bootloader dump.
*.raw
*.mff
*.bin
*.syx

# Filter-calibration recordings and fits: audio of the instrument, and large.
# The constants they produced live in src/mfemu/filter_model.py instead.
*.wav
*.pkl
# Fitted sweeps and measurement arrays: recordings of one person's
# instrument, re-derivable with filter_cal/. See filter_cal/README.md.
*.npy


__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Scratch space: anything in ignored/ stays out of git.
ignored/
.DS_Store
